  "summary": "The study fabricated five MXene electrodes: pristine HF-etched Ti3C2Tx and four N-Ti3C2Tx variants produced by post-etch NH3 annealing at 200, 300, 500, or 700 \u00b0C. The 200 \u00b0C sample was the headline and best-performing electrode, reaching 192 F g\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4 at 1 mV s\u22121; it also reached 82 F g\u22121 in 1 M MgSO4. Pristine Ti3C2Tx had its highest reported capacitance of 52 F g\u22121 in 1 M MgSO4 at 1 mV s\u22121. The paper reports XRD spacing, nitrogen content, and shared mass loading, but does not report thickness, BET surface area, porosity, pore diameter, flake lateral size, areal capacitance, or volumetric capacitance."
